# -*- mode:org;coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: navi-double-quit — NAVI's quit command should also quit ALDO
#+STATUS: DRAFT
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -

DRAFT: still needs work — capture the exact reproduction steps and
decide the intended quit semantics (one q = leave NAVI and ALDO, or
distinct commands).

DBG> Error at <toplevel> line 1 col 1 — AutoLISP builtin CLAL-SEDIT signaled an error: The file
                                               #P"/Users/pjb/src/ogamita/clautolisp/\"~/src/public/autolisp/fact.lsp\""
                                               does not exist:
                                                 No such file or directory
DBG>   <stack: <toplevel> ← top>
DBG>   (q abort, r <form> return a value, c continue/run *error*)
(DEFUN
  <toplevel>
  NIL
  【(CLAL-SEDIT (QUOTE FACT))】)
NAV> q

DBG> q

_$


The quit command of NAVI should also quit from ALDO.

* Measured 2026-09-26 (clautolisp 2.2.115) — one =q= reaches =_$=

The 2026-09-13 analysis in
=clautolisp/documentation/clautolisp-interactor-state-diagram.org= §3 concluded
from READING the code that this no longer reproduces. Now measured on the built
binary, which is what the ticket asked for ("capture the exact reproduction
steps"):

#+begin_example
$ printf '(defun foo (x) (/ x 0))\n(foo 1)\nq\ny\n(princ "AT-TOPLEVEL-AGAIN")\n(quit)\n' \
  | clautolisp -norc -q --on-error debug
_$ FOO
DBG> Error at FOO line 1 col 16 -- Division by zero in /.
DBG>   (q abort, r <form> return a value, c continue/run *error*)
(DEFUN FOO (X) [(/ X 0)])
NAV> q from the debugger aborts the execution and returns to the toplevel
NAV> really abort? (y/n)
_$ AT-TOPLEVEL-AGAIN"AT-TOPLEVEL-AGAIN"
_$ clautolisp: terminated by QUIT
$ echo $?   -> 0
#+end_example

*One =q=* (plus the y/n confirmation) goes from the navigator straight to =_$= --
the next form is read by the toplevel REPL, as the =AT-TOPLEVEL-AGAIN= echo
proves. No second =q=, and no =DBG>= prompt in between. The trace in this ticket
predates the confirm-then-abort cascade and the floor-based single-=q= return.

So the defect as reported does not reproduce, and the ticket's own sentence --
"the quit command of NAVI should also quit from ALDO" -- is what the code now
does.

*Recommendation: close as resolved-by-construction*, moving the one remaining
design question (should a single =q= ever collapse SEVERAL stacked interactors,
or always exactly one level?) into
=interactor-state-diagram-revision.issue= §4, where it belongs to the diagram
rather than to a NAVI patch. Left open because this is pjb's DRAFT ticket and
the recommendation is his to accept; the measurement above is the evidence it
was waiting for.

** A different defect found while measuring this

=(quit)= typed at the =NAV>= prompt killed the process with a 22-frame host-Lisp
backtrace and exit 1, because =AUTOLISP-TERMINATION= is a =SERIOUS-CONDITION=
that the aldo companion thread's =error= handler never saw. Filed and fixed as
=issues/closed/aldo-companion-quit-leaks-a-host-backtrace.issue= (clautolisp
2.2.116) -- it is unrelated to the quit SEMANTICS this ticket is about, which is
why it is its own ticket.

